  "dom_id": "step-q26063",
  "name": "Question 19",
  "problem": "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x)?$  Assume that $n$ is an integer.",
  "worked_solution": "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x$ is given by\n\n$$\nx\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(2x).$ This gives\n\n$$\n2x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2\\cdot 2}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2},$ where $n$ is an integer.",
